### 11. 3Sum — LeetCode #15

**Pattern:** Sorting + Two Pointers

```java
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> threeSum(int[] nums) {

        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();

        Arrays.sort(nums);

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length - 2; i++) {

            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) {
                continue;
            }

            int left = i + 1;
            int right = nums.length - 1;

            while (left < right) {

                int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];

                if (sum == 0) {

                    result.add(Arrays.asList(
                        nums[i],
                        nums[left],
                        nums[right]
                    ));

                    while (left < right &&
                           nums[left] == nums[left + 1]) {
                        left++;
                    }

                    while (left < right &&
                           nums[right] == nums[right - 1]) {
                        right--;
                    }

                    left++;
                    right--;
                }
                else if (sum < 0) {
                    left++;
                }
                else {
                    right--;
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

**Example:**

```text
Input:
[-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]

Output:
[[-1,-1,2], [-1,0,1]]
```

**Main idea:**

First sort:

```text
[-4,-1,-1,0,1,2]
```

Then:

```text
i → fixed number
left → next number
right → last number
```

If sum is:

```text
sum < 0 → left++
sum > 0 → right--
sum = 0 → answer
```

**Time:** `O(n²)`
**Space:** `O(1)` extra *(excluding output)*

